  "semantic_slots": {
    "objects": {
      "original": "Actual A_N=Fin N→Bool, actual normalized count μ_N, true sign±1, S_N=(sqrt N)^-1 sum signs, actual pushforward probability laws; literal gaussianReal0,1 target. Standardized RGO rho/r is ultimate separate context.",
      "reconstructed": "One existential family mu: N -> ProbabilityMeasure(R); its underlying Borel measures; the actual finite carriers C_n = (Fin n -> Bool); actual counting measures and their inverse-cardinality normalizations U_n; the literal maps T_n(epsilon) = (sqrt(n))^(-1) * sum_{j in Fin n} (if epsilon(j) then 1 else -1); the real-zero Dirac law; and the genuine real Gaussian law of mean 0 and variance 1. ProbabilityMeasure membership gives total mass 1 for every witness mu_n. Uniform Boolean configurations encode independent symmetric coordinate signs as a consequence of the explicit carrier law, rather than as supplied probabilistic assumptions.",
      "relation": "equivalent",
      "evidence": "Actual countLaw is inverse carrier cardinal times count, sign is Bool true1/false-1, normalizedSum and one actualLaw ProbabilityMeasure family. The public witness is that same family."
    },
    "domains": {
      "original": "Every natural N including0; successor n+1 positive for variance-one normalization. Finite discrete canonical carrier, real output/Borel weak topology, real/complex Bochner integrals genuinely finite internally.",
      "reconstructed": "Indices n range over all natural numbers, including 0. For fixed n, j ranges over Fin n = {0,...,n-1}; epsilon ranges over all Boolean functions on that whole finite index set. Counting/cardinality scaling is in ENNReal; map values, signs, sums, sqrt, and the inverse-sqrt scaling are real. Pushforwards and Dirac measures live on the real Borel space. The variance parameter of gaussianReal is the nonnegative real 1. The family and limit live in the canonical weak topology of ProbabilityMeasure(R); atTop is the natural-number tail filter.",
      "relation": "equivalent",
      "evidence": "Every natural index, finite canonical discrete measurable carrier, real Borel probability weak topology. The private generic Bochner helper uses CompleteSpace for its real/complex instantiations; this is not a public premise."
    },
    "quantifiers": {
      "original": "One actual family of laws for all N, exact map equality for all N, law0=dirac0, successor weak convergence; no random iid law, actual map identity, mean/second moment or limit supplied by a caller.",
      "reconstructed": "The outer existential quantifies one complete family mu, shared by all three conjuncts. The first conjunct universally quantifies every n in N and asserts an equality of underlying measures. The epsilon and j variables are locally bound by the pushforward map and finite sum at this same n. The second conjunct specializes the same family at n=0. In the third conjunct the locally bound sequence variable n ranges over N and selects mu_(n+1); Tendsto asserts convergence along every sufficiently large natural-number tail to the fixed Gaussian law. No free variables or quantified caller hypotheses remain. The bounded-continuous-test-function description quantifies arbitrary bounded continuous real test functions only as a semantic equivalent of the stated weak-topology convergence.",
      "relation": "equivalent",
      "evidence": "The closed theorem first produces one whole law family, then all-N map identity, its own zero law and its own successor-index limit. No ambient parameter or free variable adds a premise."
    },
    "assumptions": {
      "original": "Scalar actual-count background is unconditional apart from canonical typing. Source potential/eta assumptions stay on future SPHMC consumer; single balanced-law probability/L1/mean0/moment1 and adapters are internal obligations.",
      "reconstructed": "None at the theorem boundary: this is a closed proposition. The approved definitions fix the finite measurable structure on C_n, real Borel probabilities and their canonical weak topology, totalized real inversion, literal sign-map semantics, actual measurable pushforward, and the Gaussian mean/variance convention. They do not supply a law family or an independence, moment, central-limit, entropy, regularity, or transport certificate as a premise. The packet compiled flag is not independently checked by this decoder.",
      "relation": "equivalent",
      "evidence": "Probability, finite Bochner integrals, measurability and sign mean/secondmoment are internally derived. The scalar CLT consumes sign_mean/sign_second_moment, not caller certificates."
    },
    "conclusion": {
      "original": "Only actual law family and weak gaussianReal0,1 convergence; no entropy/energy/LSI/T2/W2/main/cost output.",
      "reconstructed": "There exists a family of genuine probabilities whose underlying measures equal the explicit normalized-counting pushforward for every n >= 0, whose zero member is exactly delta_0, and whose sequence of positive-index members mu_(n+1) tends weakly to N(0,1). All three claims refer to the same existential family. The limit is weak probability-law convergence, not convergence of sampled values, densities, moments, total variation, entropy, or a transport metric; no rate is asserted.",
      "relation": "equivalent",
      "evidence": "Actual count integrals and exp_sum/sum_pow produce finite characteristic-function factorization; scalar CLT plus Levy gives weak convergence, then cofinal n+1 composition. No stronger convergence conclusion."
    },
    "scopes": {
      "original": "External SLT real product has NeZero N and no Boolean-count/N0 result. Direct finite-count factorization and finite real-product transport are authored alternatives. Infinite-iid route has genuine construction/prefix-law gaps. Existing compiled Mathlib scalar leaf is not ASTIS producer.",
      "reconstructed": "The universal n in the first conjunct does not bind the other conjuncts; their zero index and separate successor-indexed lambda are explicit. At n=0 the carrier is a singleton, normalization is inverse 1, sum is empty, and (sqrt(0))^(-1)=0, so the map sends its sole configuration to real zero. For positive n the scale is 1/sqrt(n), multiplying the entire signed sum with true -> +1 and false -> -1. The limit lambda uses n+1 both when selecting the family and, through that family member identity, in its carrier and normalization: its configuration count is 2^(n+1) and its scale is 1/sqrt(n+1). The finite counting normalization uses the actual number of configurations, not n. The limit Gaussian and its mean 0/variance 1 are fixed outside all sequence variables. ProbabilityMeasure weak neighborhoods are used, not an unspecified topology on raw measures.",
      "relation": "equivalent",
      "evidence": "All-N map equality includes0. totalized inverse0 and empty sum give actualLaw_zero. Same family uses n+1 consistently. Actual finite-count adapter is authored background, distinct from external SLT product/infinite-iid gaps."
    },
    "constant_dependencies": {
      "original": "Actual mass2^-N, normalization1/sqrt N, variance1 Gaussian. N0 second moment0. Future full-flip factor4 and finite half-to-Gaussian2 energy transfer are external residuals, not consequences of weak CLT.",
      "reconstructed": "All objects depend solely on their explicit index n and fixed definitions. Carrier cardinal N_n=2^n and U_n normalization 1/2^n depend on n; T_n depends on n and epsilon, with fixed signs +1 and -1 and real inverse-square-root scaling. The zero Dirac location is fixed at 0. The Gaussian mean is fixed 0 and its variance is fixed 1 (hence standard deviation 1); no n-dependent Gaussian, auxiliary parameter, hidden constant, convergence rate, or caller data occurs. No external theorem or proof body is consulted.",
      "relation": "equivalent",
      "evidence": "Actual mass2^-N, scale inverse sqrtN, signs±1, internally derived coordinate mean0/secondmoment1 and fixed Gaussian0/variance1. N0 secondmoment0 retained; no rate, flip4, entropy or GaussianLSI constant follows."
    }
  },
